{"755871":{"pv":["MB"],"km":3998,"cr":"1985-07-18","iucn":"II","site":"https://www.gov.mb.ca/sd/parks/park-maps-and-locations/eastern/atikaki.fr.html","wp":"en:Atikaki_Provincial_Wilderness_Park"},"795190":{"pv":["MB"],"km":2969,"cr":"1930","iucn":"II","site":"http://www.pc.gc.ca/fra/pn-np/mb/riding/index.aspx","wp":"en:Riding_Mountain_National_Park","f":[["Bison herd - Lake Audy - Riding Mountain National Park.JPG","Norm Andreiw","CC BY 3.0"],["Escarpment to prairie sea - RMNP.jpg","Krazytea","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["East Gate RMNP.jpg","Krazytea","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Riding Mountain National Park, Wasagaming (340305) (9444527460).jpg","Robert Linsdell from St. Andrews, Canada","CC BY 2.0"],["Overlooking farmland from the Manitoba Escarpment in Riding Mountain National Park in Manitoba, Canada. (37638852151).jpg","Rob Swystun from Winnipeg, Canada","CC BY 2.0"]],"t":{"pt":{"r":"No alto da Riding Mountain, na escarpa de Manitoba: uma ilha de floresta no meio das fazendas da pradaria. Ali se encontram pradaria, floresta boreal e floresta decídua do leste.","h":"Virou parque nacional em 1930. A vila de Wasagaming, na entrada sul, é o único centro comercial dentro do parque, e a área é o núcleo de uma Reserva da Biosfera da UNESCO.","ff":"Uma das maiores populações de ursos-negros da América do Norte, além de uapitis, alces, lobos, linces, castores e bisões; 233 espécies de aves e 669 de plantas.","at":["Clear Lake e a vila de Wasagaming","Manada de bisões do lago Audy","Mais de 400 km de trilhas","Esqui de fundo e raquetes de neve no inverno"]},"en":{"r":"Atop Riding Mountain on the Manitoba Escarpment: an island of forest amid prairie farmland, where grassland, boreal forest and eastern deciduous forest meet.","h":"It became a national park in 1930. The townsite of Wasagaming, at the south entrance, is the only commercial centre inside the park, which is the core of a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve.","ff":"One of North America's largest black bear populations, plus elk, moose, wolves, lynx, beavers and bison; 233 bird species and 669 plant species.","at":["Clear Lake and Wasagaming","The Lake Audy bison herd","More than 400 km of trails","Cross-country skiing and snowshoeing in winter"]},"es":{"r":"En lo alto de la Riding Mountain, en la escarpa de Manitoba: una isla de bosque entre granjas de pradera, donde se encuentran pradera, bosque boreal y bosque caducifolio del este.","h":"Pasó a ser parque nacional en 1930. El pueblo de Wasagaming, en la entrada sur, es el único centro comercial dentro del parque, núcleo de una Reserva de la Biosfera de la UNESCO.","ff":"Una de las mayores poblaciones de osos negros de América del Norte, además de uapitíes, alces, lobos, linces, castores y bisontes; 233 especies de aves y 669 de plantas.","at":["Clear Lake y Wasagaming","La manada de bisontes del lago Audy","Más de 400 km de senderos","Esquí de fondo y raquetas de nieve en invierno"]}}},"1571016":{"pv":["MB"],"km":1084,"cr":"1969-01-01","iucn":"II","site":"https://gov.mb.ca/sd/parks/park-maps-and-locations/central/hecla.fr.html","wp":"en:Hecla-Grindstone_Provincial_Park","f":[["Hecla Island and Provincial Park in Lake Winnipeg Manitoba (14).JPG","Shahnoor Habib Munmun","CC BY 3.0"],["Gull Harbour, Hecla Island - panoramio.jpg","Bob Linsdell","CC BY 3.0"],["Grassy Narrows Marsh, Hecla Island - panoramio.jpg","Bob Linsdell","CC BY 3.0"],["Grassy Narrows, Hecla Island - panoramio.jpg","Bob Linsdell","CC BY 3.0"],["Gull Harbour, Hecla Island - panoramio (1).jpg","Bob Linsdell","CC BY 3.0"]]},"1638019":{"pv":["MB"],"km":11475,"cr":"1996","iucn":"II","site":"http://www.pc.gc.ca/pn-np/mb/wapusk.aspx","wp":"en:Wapusk_National_Park","f":[["Bärenmutter & Junges 3 2004-11-17.jpg","Ansgar Walk","CC BY 2.5"],["Cape Churchill 2000-11-22.jpg","Ansgar Walk","CC BY 2.5"],["Geburtshöhlen 1999-07-02.jpg","Ansgar Walk","CC BY 2.5"],["Knight's Hill 2000-11-22.jpg","Ansgar Walk","CC BY 2.5"],["Wapusk 2 1996-08-12.jpg","Ansgar Walk","CC BY 2.5"]],"t":{"pt":{"r":"Na costa da baía de Hudson, em Manitoba, 45 km ao sul de Churchill. O nome vem da palavra cree para urso-polar, e o cabo Churchill é considerado o melhor lugar do mundo para ver e fotografar ursos-polares selvagens.","h":"Criado em 1996, 37º parque nacional do Canadá, para proteger a natureza e as tradições cree. É território tradicional das Primeiras Nações cree de York Factory e Fox Lake, dos sayisi dene e dos inuítes.","ff":"Uma das maiores áreas de tocas de ursos-polares do mundo. A quebra do gelo marinho até três semanas mais cedo, por causa do aquecimento, já afeta a reprodução dos ursos.","at":["Ursos-polares no cabo Churchill, só de helicóptero ou veículo de tundra","Visitas às tocas em fevereiro e março, com operadores autorizados","Tundra costeira, morainas e eskers da última glaciação"]},"en":{"r":"On the Hudson Bay coast of Manitoba, 45 km south of Churchill. The name comes from the Cree word for polar bear, and Cape Churchill is considered the world's best place to see and photograph wild polar bears.","h":"Established in 1996 as Canada's 37th national park, to protect nature and Cree traditions. It is traditional territory of the York Factory and Fox Lake Cree, the Sayisi Dene and the Inuit.","ff":"One of the world's largest polar bear denning areas. Sea ice now breaks up as much as three weeks earlier because of warming, which is already affecting the bears' reproduction.","at":["Polar bears at Cape Churchill, by helicopter or tundra vehicle only","Den viewing in February and March with licensed operators","Coastal tundra, moraines and eskers from the last ice age"]},"es":{"r":"En la costa de la bahía de Hudson, en Manitoba, 45 km al sur de Churchill. El nombre viene de la palabra cree para oso polar, y el cabo Churchill se considera el mejor lugar del mundo para ver y fotografiar osos polares salvajes.","h":"Creado en 1996 como 37.º parque nacional de Canadá, para proteger la naturaleza y las tradiciones cree. Es territorio tradicional de los cree de York Factory y Fox Lake, de los sayisi dene y de los inuit.","ff":"Una de las mayores zonas de madrigueras de osos polares del mundo. El hielo marino se rompe hasta tres semanas antes por el calentamiento, lo que ya afecta la reproducción de los osos.","at":["Osos polares en el cabo Churchill, solo en helicóptero o vehículo de tundra","Visitas a las madrigueras en febrero y marzo con operadores autorizados","Tundra costera, morrenas y eskers de la última glaciación"]}}},"1659649":{"pv":["MB"],"km":6.7,"cr":"2001-01-01","iucn":"III","site":"http://www.gov.mb.ca/conservation/parks/popular_parks/central/pembina.html","wp":"en:Pembina_Valley_Provincial_Park","f":[["Pembina valley provincial park cranberry hollow.jpg","Darethehair","CC BY-SA 3.0"],["Pembina Valley Provincial Park, Manitoba, Canada (29451211414).jpg","Rob Swystun from Winnipeg, Canada","CC BY 2.0"],["Pembina River in Pembina Valley PP.jpg","Words in the Wind","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Pembina Valley Panorama Point South 2.jpg","Words in the Wind","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Pembina Valley Panorama Point South.jpg","Words in the Wind","CC BY-SA 4.0"]]},"1996516":{"pv":["MB"],"km":1429,"cr":"1976-04-20","iucn":"II","wp":"en:Nopiming_Provincial_Park","f":[["Sunset Nopiming Provincial Park MB Canada.jpg","Nandreiw","CC BY-SA 4.0"]]},"2567111":{"pv":["MB"],"km":2752,"cr":"1961-06-01","iucn":"II","site":"https://www.gov.mb.ca/sd/parks/park-maps-and-locations/eastern/whiteshell.fr.html","wp":"en:Whiteshell_Provincial_Park","f":[["Falcon Lake, Whiteshell Provincial Park (181113533).jpg","Jon Eben Field from Vancouver, BC, Canada","CC BY 2.0"],["Open view of Whiteshell River, to the left a rocky granite shore.jpg","Ethan Sahagun","CC BY-SA 3.0"],["Whiteshell Provincial Park.jpg","Ethan Sahagun","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Whiteshell Natural History Museum Manitoba.JPG","qwekiop147","CC BY 3.0"],["West hawk lake biking.jpg","","Domínio público"]]},"3364704":{"pv":["MB"],"km":35.1,"cr":"1964-04-06","iucn":"III","site":"https://www.gov.mb.ca/sd/parks/par